Description: Keep what each state read when the input ends
 At the end of the input the HTML tokenizer emits the text, comment or
 raw text it has read. The data, comment and raw-text states, and the
 attribute name and value states, now push what they read as their token
 through one helper. Upstream dropped it, so the rest of a file after an
 unterminated "<!--" or "<script>" was in no node, and the data state's
 range left out a trailing "<".
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/parse-for-eslint.test.ts ("unquoted attribute values"); test/parser/diagnostics.test.ts
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
